WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.840
You’ve been walking for days. Your body aches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.640
you’re dripping with sweat from the heat&nbsp;
of the sun bearing down overhead. And yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.680
you’re wrapped up in layers upon layers&nbsp;
of clothing - even your face is covered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.760
and you’re wearing thick, black goggles so that&nbsp;
not a single centimeter of your body is exposed.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.600
Your journey has been long and you feel like you&nbsp;
might die from exhaustion, or from overheating due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:32.160
to these multiple layers of clothes. But dying&nbsp;
is better than being exposed. You saw it happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:41.200
when your entire team...changed. The light can’t&nbsp;
be trusted. Not even for a fraction of a second.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.640
It’s been like this for years. You’ve learned&nbsp;
and survived through painful experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:52.800
Many of those you used to know cannot say&nbsp;
the same. You’ve been alone for so long.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.080
You might have given up all hope, if it wasn’t&nbsp;
for the distress signal coming from a nearby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:05.600
SCP Foundation Containment Facility - Site-46. Any&nbsp;
kind of survivors would be better than nothing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:11.920
no matter what kind of sorry shape they&nbsp;
were in. As long as they were still human.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:17.840
You find your way to an opening in the side of&nbsp;
a mountain, and slide into the cave, hoping you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:24.800
weren’t spotted. The whole world is crawling with&nbsp;
those things now. You can’t let yourself be seen.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:29.360
As you trudge down the cave towards the&nbsp;
entrance, you see what looks like a huge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:35.200
black snail-trail splattered on the ground,&nbsp;
leading into the facility. You try to avoid it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:41.440
and press on. You don’t even need a keycard&nbsp;
to enter: The door has been left ajar.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:46.160
The facility reeks of those things,&nbsp;
but you can’t see any of them. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.480
just hope they’ve moved on and left&nbsp;
some human survivors in their wake.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:56.480
The place looks abandoned. Every step&nbsp;
you take echoes through the empty halls.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:02.080
When you find that the elevator’s out, you&nbsp;
take the stairs all the way down to Level B5…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.280
Keter Containment. Lucky for you, it&nbsp;
seems all the cells are empty now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:12.080
the horrors that were kept inside of&nbsp;
them have all long since flown the coop.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.280
You keep following that slimy, black&nbsp;
trail until you find an abandoned office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:23.120
There are no people here anymore - just a&nbsp;
broken barricade, some empty medicine bottles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.320
and a bucket that the people inside the&nbsp;
office had apparently been using as a toilet.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.160
You breathe a sigh of disappointment&nbsp;
at finding no one alive here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:38.400
but you’re at least relieved to be out of the sun.&nbsp;
You can finally remove your jacket and head-wrap.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.520
With your uncovered eyes, you notice that a&nbsp;
nearby computer terminal is still powered up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:48.240
You sit down at the desk and turn on the&nbsp;
monitor. Because of the Emergency Procedures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:54.640
put into place in a K-Class scenario like this,&nbsp;
safeguards no longer apply. You can access&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:03:00.240
all the information you need - up to and&nbsp;
including finding out what actually happened.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:06.240
In the dull glow of a nearby emergency light, you&nbsp;
see a dark shape slumping through the halls in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:13.760
shadow. You tense up, then exhale as it slithers&nbsp;
off into an adjoining hall. You’re safe - for now.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.520
The terminal has finally loaded&nbsp;
and authenticated your access.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:23.200
You’re staring at the file for&nbsp;
S.D. Locke’s Proposal for SCP-001:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.720
When Day Breaks. It’s the only name you can&nbsp;
give the apocalypse your world is currently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.880
experiencing. This is one of the only anomalies&nbsp;
in the entire history of the SCP Foundation to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:41.920
be given the Apollyon containment class -&nbsp;
meaning containment is truly impossible.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.160
SCP-001 is the most dangerous&nbsp;
enemy that the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:51.440
and planet earth, has ever faced. It’s always&nbsp;
been a principle of the SCP Foundation to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:56.240
battle in the dark so that the civilian&nbsp;
world can thrive in the light, but now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:02.720
the light has become the enemy. Anyone exposed&nbsp;
to any amount of sunlight for even the briefest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:10.640
period of time is subjected to the effects of&nbsp;
SCP-001 - and those effects are beyond horrifying.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.760
The SCP Foundation Administrator released an&nbsp;
urgent memo telling Foundation personnel to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:22.160
their way to Site-19 at all costs, because they&nbsp;
need all the help they can get. Those exposed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:31.280
SCP-001 in the process are no longer considered&nbsp;
human - their new designation is SCP-001-A. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:38.960
new entities are to be avoided at all costs. But,&nbsp;
in case of emergencies, the Administrator says it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:44.880
is permitted to cut off parts of your transformed&nbsp;
comrades and eat them to avoid starvation.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:51.120
No attempt should be made to kill them, since you&nbsp;
won’t succeed, you’ll just put yourself at risk.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:57.840
When the sun changed and became SCP-001,&nbsp;
it instantly affected 6.8 billion innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.800
people. The second the visible light touched&nbsp;
them - whether it was from the sun itself or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:09.120
reflected off the moon - their bodies liquefied,&nbsp;
melting like candle wax into puddles of living,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:15.440
gelatinous slime. This effect isn’t isolated&nbsp;
to humans, either: Any biological entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:24.160
exposed to sunlight immediately underwent the&nbsp;
same irreversible melting process into SCP-001-A.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.600
And the horror had only just begun.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:33.280
People transformed into SCP-001-A will retain&nbsp;
shades of their former intelligence and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:38.960
personality. They may even try to will their&nbsp;
new gooey mass into a shape resembling their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:44.000
original form. However, these individuals&nbsp;
will lose their sense of self if they come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:50.320
into contact with other instances of&nbsp;
SCP-001-A. When they come together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:56.080
001-A instances will bond on a molecular&nbsp;
level, wadding up into horrific,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:02.240
giant blobs with only one purpose:&nbsp;
Integrating more matter into their bodies.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.920
That’s why they have to be avoided at all costs.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.120
You continue to search the&nbsp;
computer terminal for answers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.880
Perhaps there was some kind of&nbsp;
contingency plan put in place for this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:18.400
Some way to reverse the effects, or at&nbsp;
least escape the nightmare Earth has become.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:24.160
Instead, you find a series of attachments&nbsp;
linked to the SCP-001 file, detailing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:29.040
what seems to be the last days of the people&nbsp;
who’d barricaded themselves in the facility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.560
Most prominent among these were&nbsp;
Researcher Dr. Logan Igotta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:38.800
her partner, Ari, a security officer named&nbsp;
Commander Anand, and a few others. Dr. Igotta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:44.080
had locked herself in the office, where she&nbsp;
recorded her final messages to the world.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:49.760
In the first audio log, Dr. Igotta and her&nbsp;
companions seemed afraid but hopeful that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.440
may be some way out of this situation. Dr. Igotta&nbsp;
reported that most of the workers at the facility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:01.680
were transformed during the initial event. Their&nbsp;
melted bodies had fused outside the facility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.800
and now they were trying&nbsp;
to bust their way back in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:08.720
The defenses had held so far though,&nbsp;
and they seemed confident they would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:13.280
hold long enough for them to figure out&nbsp;
a way to escape this awful situation.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.000
You open the second attachment - an incident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:21.200
report - and realize that things may not&nbsp;
have been as hopeful as Dr. Igotta let on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:26.400
She reported hearing the huge mass of melted&nbsp;
creatures hammering on the door outside again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.280
begging for them to come out and experience&nbsp;
the sun with them. They wanted desperately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:36.800
to add to their ever-growing biomass. In order&nbsp;
to experiment with what exactly would happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:42.000
they sent out one of their few remaining&nbsp;
D-Classes wearing a full protective suit.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.760
He didn’t last long.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:47.920
The huge creature grabbed him with&nbsp;
tentacles made of reconstituted flesh.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:53.520
It began ripping off his protective suit as&nbsp;
he screamed for mercy. It was a monster made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.520 --> 00:08:00.240
of dozens of people and animals. He could never&nbsp;
overpower it. The second the sun touched his skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:05.600
he melted away, and was absorbed by&nbsp;
the great mass holding him in place.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:10.640
Guns were ineffective against&nbsp;
these SCP-001-A super-entities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.280
Fire would do no good. It seemed that&nbsp;
extremely low temperatures were the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:21.280
only way to slow the immense blobs&nbsp;
down, and even then, not permanently.

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:26.960
There was one ray of light in the darkness: The&nbsp;
Site Director had a secret tunnel underneath his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:32.240
office, connected to a tram that could hopefully&nbsp;
take them directly to Site 19 without risk of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:39.360
SCP-001 exposure. It was a good plan, and by&nbsp;
far the best option they had available to them.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:43.200
But the best plans often don’t work in practice.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:49.360
You open the next attachment on the terminal. This&nbsp;
time, it’s a video feed. You can actually see Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:55.040
Logan Igotta - and she looks harrowed by what&nbsp;
she’s experienced. As it turns out, while the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.040 --> 00:09:00.560
others, including her partner Ari, attempted to&nbsp;
exit through the tunnel something had happened.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:06.640
Dr. Igotta heard Ari’s voice over her radio. But&nbsp;
there was something wrong with it. It was too low.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:13.920
Too guttural. And filled with gurgles.&nbsp;
SCP-001 had gotten to her. She was changed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:20.000
The monster from above had crawled in through&nbsp;
the ceiling. It had taken them, all of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:26.720
and converted them into something less than&nbsp;
human. Any hope of escape now seemed gone.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:32.720
Ari told Dr. Igotta that it would be fine. That it&nbsp;
was such a bright, beautiful, sunny day outside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:37.920
and she was wasting it locked up inside that&nbsp;
office. She tormented Dr. Igotta with their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:42.960
shared memories of picnics in the park on&nbsp;
sunny days in the past. The monster with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:48.320
Ari’s voice did everything it could to try to&nbsp;
convince Dr. Igotta to give up and join them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.120
but she wasn’t ready to go just yet.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.720
You look away from the screen when&nbsp;
you hear a sound in the corner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:58.400
You see a dark puddle of some&nbsp;
unknown substance, and then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.280
some skeletal hands rising out of it. The&nbsp;
hands are pulling themselves out of the puddle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:08.960
followed by a skeletal face covered in matted&nbsp;
hair. You have to stop yourself from screaming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:15.520
until a flash from a nearby security light makes&nbsp;
the figure disappear. It’s a normal puddle again.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:17.760
Your mind is playing tricks on you.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:24.160
You open the next attachment, another video, and&nbsp;
see that Dr. Igotta’s condition has deteriorated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:29.440
She looked pale, frantic, and thin. She&nbsp;
was using a knife to draw her own blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:35.440
onto a piece of bloodstained parchment covered in&nbsp;
strange symbols. Igotta ranted about her theory:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:40.640
What if 001 took the minds and bodies&nbsp;
of its victims, but not their souls?

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.440
Through performing some&nbsp;
kind of arcane blood ritual,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:49.280
she hoped to at least rescue and keep the soul&nbsp;
of Ari, even if her mind and body were lost.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:54.320
You open the next attachment. It seems that&nbsp;
Igotta’s ritual worked, but not in the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.320 --> 00:11:01.520
she hoped. The twisted soul of Ari, driven mad&nbsp;
by SCP-001, had taken over the file. It begins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:07.840
corrupting the text of the SCP-001 file into&nbsp;
crazy ranting about how futile it is to fight.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:11.120
It then cut to an even more&nbsp;
frightening video feed:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:17.120
Dr. Igotta in her sleep, tossing and turning&nbsp;
in a makeshift bed in the corner of her office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:22.800
The camera approaches her, in first&nbsp;
person, and lingers over her sleeping body.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:26.080
An oily, skeletal hand reaches past the camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:31.280
and runs its fingers through Dr. Igotta’s&nbsp;
hair. It’s the exact same hand you saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:37.120
reaching out of that black puddle earlier.&nbsp;
You must have seen Ari’s lingering spirit.

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:42.320
With a lump in your throat, you open&nbsp;
the next attachment and watch the video.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:49.200
You see Dr. Igotta, now truly broken. She’d been&nbsp;
haunted by Ari’s demonic spirit for a long time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:54.720
now, and it has clearly taken its toll. She&nbsp;
is waving around a handgun while she speaks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:57.760
She now believes there is only one way to escape.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:02.240
But not like this. She doesn’t want&nbsp;
the gun to draw attention to her body.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:08.000
She doesn’t want to become part of that mass, even&nbsp;
if she is dead. She opens a drawer on the desk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:13.760
she’s recording at and places the gun inside.&nbsp;
Dr. Igotta then apologizes to her loved ones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:20.080
who are likely long since dead or assimilated,&nbsp;
and turns off the recording for the last time.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:25.280
In that moment, you realize that there’s a single&nbsp;
drawer in the desk in front of you. When you reach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:31.760
forward and open it, you see that the same handgun&nbsp;
Dr. Igotta was holding is laying inside. You pick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:37.920
it up and study it, weighing up your options.&nbsp;
Perhaps there truly is no other way out...

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:40.000
Then, you see an update on the file.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:43.280
One more attachment had been added&nbsp;
while you were studying the gun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:48.560
You feel your heart pounding in your chest&nbsp;
as you reach forward and open the attachment.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:56.960
The text has been changed entirely. The file&nbsp;
on SCP-001 is now a poem - an ode to the sun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:02.560
and to ultimate togetherness. Then a&nbsp;
video file spontaneously opens itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:08.320
on the screen: It’s a video of you,&nbsp;
shot from behind. You see those oily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:13.600
skeletal hands reaching for you in the&nbsp;
dark, just like they did with Dr. Igotta.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:18.960
In that moment, you panic and fire the gun&nbsp;
behind you, hoping to scare off the spirit.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:23.280
Instead, the sound of the gunshots&nbsp;
attracts something far worse.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:28.320
The immense blob of screaming, melted flesh&nbsp;
charges towards the office. You try to barricade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:33.680
the door, but it’s not enough. The flesh seeps&nbsp;
and bursts through, and grabs you in its meaty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:41.120
tentacles. You scream and try to escape, but&nbsp;
it won’t save you. Nothing will save you.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:44.960
The flesh carries you upstairs,&nbsp;
out through the empty halls, out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:49.840
into the cave. You can see the light in the&nbsp;
distance as the blob ferries you towards it.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:56.160
You won’t be alone for much longer. In&nbsp;
fact, you won’t be alone ever again...

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:59.760
Now check out “SCP-001 - The Scarlet King”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:09.440
and “SCP-001 - Which is the real 001?” for more&nbsp;
deep dives into SCP-001 mysteries and lore!

